+# To-do app
+
+A single static page (`src/index.html` + `src/app.js`), no build step and no server. Tasks are stored in the browser's `localStorage`, so they are per browser profile and per origin.
+
+## Run
+
+Open `src/index.html` directly (it is a classic script, not an ES module, because Chrome blocks module scripts on `file://`), or `pnpm start` to serve `src/` at http://127.0.0.1:4173.
+
+## Test
+
+`pnpm install` once, then `pnpm test`. Playwright runs `tests/todo.spec.mjs` and `tests/file.spec.mjs` against real Chromium in desktop and mobile (Pixel 7) viewports, serving `src/` with the dependency-free `tests/serve.mjs`. Tests fail on page errors and block any request that leaves the local server.
+
+Covered: add (trimmed; blank and whitespace-only rejected with a message), Enter-to-add, complete/incomplete toggle, delete of one task among several, order and state after reload, task text rendered as text (not HTML), recovery from corrupt storage, storage write failure (error shown, nothing changes), focus after delete, loading from `file://`, no horizontal overflow. The screenshot test writes `test-results/*/{desktop,mobile}.png` for visual review.
+
+## Storage format
+
+Key `todo.tasks.v1`: JSON array of `{ id: string, text: string, done: boolean }`. On load, invalid JSON or a non-array resets to empty; entries with a missing id or blank text are dropped, and text is trimmed; `done` is true only if stored as `true`. Bump the key suffix if the shape changes incompatibly.
+
+Every change is written to storage before the UI adopts it; if the write throws (quota, private mode, disabled storage), the change is discarded and an error is shown.
